Now I need to check what happens after `idprime_get_token_name` returns 0. The caller does:
```c
r = sc_card_ctl(card, SC_CARDCTL_IDPRIME_GET_TOKEN_NAME, &token_name);
if (r < 0) {
    /* failure path */
} else {
    free(p15card->tokeninfo->label);  // frees "IDPrime"
    p15card->tokeninfo->label = token_name;  // stores dangling pointer
    sc_log(card->ctx, "IDPrime setting token label = %s", token_name);  // UAF read
}
```

Then it continues to `SC_CARDCTL_IDPRIME_INIT_GET_OBJECTS`. Let me check what that does - it might also need APDU responses.

